  "definition": "The end-to-end progression of an application programming interface from design and specification through implementation, publication, versioning, monitoring, deprecation, and eventual retirement. Managing the API lifecycle as a deliberate process \u2014 with contract-first design, semantic versioning, sunset policies, and consumer migration paths \u2014 is what keeps evolving service interfaces stable for the clients that depend on them.",
